legal_descriptions.courses_verbatim:
ALL that certain plot, piece or parcel of land, situate, lying and being in the Borough of Manhattan, County, City and State of New York, being part of certain premises, which on a partition between Jacob Horn and others, as heirs or devisees of John Horn, deceased, were allotted to the said Jacob Horn, as his part, and distinguished on a map filed in December 1816, by the Commissioners, of Partition, in the Office of the Register of the City and County of New York, by the No. 1, said premises being distinguished on a map made by J.F. Bridges, City Surveyor and filed in the Office of the Register aforesaid (marked 121) in February 1829 by the No. 10 and 11, bounded and described as follows, to wit:

BEGINNING at a point on the southerly side of West 25th Street, at the distance of 225 feet westerly from the westerly side of Sixth Avenue, (now known as Avenue of the Americas);

RUNNING THENCE southerly at right angles to said West 25th Street, 81 feet 9 inches more or less to the boundary line which on said partition map separates said Jacob Horn's portion from Matthew Dikeman's portion;

THENCE westerly along said boundary line on said map, and on a line which forms on its northerly side of an angle of 89 degrees 31 minutes 20 seconds with the last course 50 feet;

THENCE northerly on a line parallel with the first course and along the dividing line between Lot 11 and Lot 12 on said Map and part of the distance through a party wall to the southerly side of West 25th Street, 81 feet 4 inches more or less to the southerly side of West 25th Street;

THENCE easterly along said southerly side of 25th Street, 50 feet to the point or place of BEGINNING.

ALL that certain plot, piece or parcel of land, situate, lying and being in the Borough of Manhattan, County, City and State of New York, bounded and described as follows:

BEGINNING at a point on the southerly side of West 25th Street, distant 275 feet westerly from the corner formed by the intersection of the southerly side of West 25th Street and the westerly side of Sixth Avenue (now known as Avenue of the Americas);

RUNNING THENCE southerly parallel with Sixth Avenue, 98 feet 9 inches to the center line of the block;

THENCE westerly along said center line of the block, 25 feet;

THENCE northerly parallel with Sixth Avenue, 98 feet 9 inches to the southerly side of 25th Street;

THENCE easterly along the southerly side of 25th Street, 25 feet to the point or place of BEGINNING.

ALL that certain plot, piece or parcel of land, situate, lying and being in the Borough of Manhattan, Country, City and State of New York, bounded and described as follows:

BEGINNING at a point on the southerly side of West 25th Street, distant 300 feet westerly from the corner formed by the intersection of the southerly side of 25th Street and the westerly side of Sixth Avenue (now known as Avenue of the Americas);

RUNNING THENCE southerly parallel with Sixth Avenue, and part of the distance through a party wall, 98 feet 9 inches to the center line of the block;

THENCE westerly along the center line of the block, 25 feet;

THENCE northerly parallel with Sixth Avenue, 98 feet 9 inches to the southerly side of West 25th Street;

THENCE easterly along the southerly side of West 25th Street, 25 feet to the point or place of BEGINNING.

ALL that certain plot, piece or parcel of land, situate, lying and being in the Borough of Manhattan of the City of New York, known as and by the street numbers 112-118 West 25th Street and 113-117 West 24th Street, and more particularly bounded and described as follows:

BEGINNING at a point on the southerly side of 25th Street distant 140 feet westerly from the corner formed by the intersection of the westerly side of 6th Avenue with the southerly side of 25th Street;

THENCE southerly parallel with the westerly side of 6th Avenue and through a party wall  about 82 feet 8 3/4 inches to the boundary line which on the partition map filed December, 1816 in New York County Register's Office by Commissioners of Partition Separates Jacob Horn's portion from Matthew Dikeman's portion;

THENCE westerly along the said boundary line 10 feet;

THENCE southerly parallel with the westerly side of 6th Avenue 114 feet 10 inches more or less to the northerly side of 24th Street;

THENCE westerly along the northerly side of 24th street 75 feet;

THENCE northerly parallel with the westerly side of 6th Avenue 197 feet 6 inches to the southerly side of 25th Street; and

THENCE easterly along the southerly side of 25th Street 85 feet to the point or place of BEGINNING.
